      <workList xml:id="workDesc_599379a1">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e180177">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_8dae9758">A1:003</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_13" xml:lang="it">Concerto a flauto, 2 violini, alto e basso</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_d02e2798">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_15">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_16_0">
               <p xml:id="idm76">The only information on the present concerto is from a catalogue of <persName xml:id="idm77" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Nicolas Selhof</persName>'s auction held in Amsterdam 1759. It is possible that the work might be identical to one of those which have survived (SchW A1:001, A1:002, A1:005, A1:006, A1:007). The work was in manuscript. It seems unlikely that it was obtained from the Breitkopf publishers in Leipzig as their earliest catalogues for works is from 1761 when they acquired the large music collection amassed by the cantor of Neukirche, <persName xml:id="idm78" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Carl Gotthelf Gerlach</persName>. Thus it seems likely that <persName xml:id="idm79" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Selhof</persName> obtained a copy directly from the composer.</p>
            </history>
